{"title":"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Some_trial_and_error)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Some trial and error)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(More_Robust_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (More Robust Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sequences of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/0328a2934c48b8eda8571791664f0a528ec479f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,a_2, a_3,...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/7/ec71582c00eadfa12deac83a43feb345d2fc8ef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,b_2, b_3,...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> are an increasing arithmetic sequence and an increasing geometric sequence, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c0347f07cfe011112f35133df69e8d06db1e04a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_n=a_n+b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"15\" />. There is an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6dcec6bd03d0d877fbf89048c2d347e64a2aba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_{k-1}=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/205c74550449b41a569d28acf14290ad9cd55ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_{k+1}=1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd87559f4e4c9af40246a0fdbafe6feab507414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since all the terms of the sequences are integers, and 100 isn't very big, we should just try out the possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b7aa611365e135f58aa09d52043ecd34855fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />. When we get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f75799f8c2cec837f972e89b8a99eedeecde97d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132adb28bd675924faeb12ddcce55364684c5f6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4a87259c72ea42070340e61dc8f549d181752c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4=271$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbbff689a3fb7a8d01bd9f6b5fa87eddb866d632.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_4=729$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />, which works, therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/630012c3e7bce888046634f550464bbde38be961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_3+a_3=81+181=\\boxed{262}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Some_trial_and_error.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Some_trial_and_error)\">Solution 2 (Some trial and error)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Some trial and error)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1a8598c4d89f65f0fc30aef15e43228ec83226.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k=r^{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f95b581bc7f4217ec6dd6d1e628a8eab0a6d1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k=(k-1)d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />. First, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45fb5b37dc54caca5ed185ee59c6cf629b07dbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k-1}&lt;c_{k-1}=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/b/e4b076f21c4bfb955981a9e38d204a98248a624c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d&lt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/f/98fb501710de47409c7eb1314c71c39079e290d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+1}&lt;300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f391b172236f8209664743c68f4968450ffca33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1}=1000-b_{k+1}&gt;700$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" />, i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/0/ca0f0f2d1d7f49f4725eb277582f4c191505f308.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[700 &lt; r^k &lt; 1000.\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" /> Moreover, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is atleast <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/e/86ed0d8efa33684908fe2314f898ab037ec3fc68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^3\\le r^k &lt;1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e4b8cd1edfcf017e240c65a155c39957f4926a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&lt;10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />. For every value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> in this range, define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3badf3f47042e5fe4b9cb62b5df495ff0113b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i(r) = \\max \\{x : r^x &lt; 700\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"201\" height=\"20\" />, and define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/c/f6c2d0412e82e8c6f553641094e183a53fffc3d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j(r) = \\min \\{x : r^x &gt; 1000\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"20\" />. We are looking for values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb4c2e610eabfd86afdb89ab4ef1d26ba62831de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j(r) -i(r)&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />. Let's make a table:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b48d9a01647e46bd053abba6e2d9734d6b41127.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{array}[b]{ c c c c c c c c c } r &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 &amp; 6 &amp; 7 &amp; 8 &amp; 9 \\\\[2ex] i(r) &amp; 9  &amp; 5 &amp; 4  &amp; 4 &amp; 3 &amp; 3 &amp; 3 &amp; 2\\\\[2ex] j(r) &amp; 10  &amp; 7 &amp; 5  &amp; 5 &amp; 4 &amp; 4 &amp; 4 &amp; 4 \\end{array}\" width=\"246\" height=\"86\" />\nThe only admissible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcdc1537798e37cfc7e1ac90e2b0d36a1e31f55a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^k$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32fa79de8da8e01f46f2b7ba42686f3ae020d55b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{3^6, 9^3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"21\" />. However, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/707609a03aa1d7ab22d2bb4976214b5b2fa49652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100=c_{k-1}=r^{k-2}+(k-2)d+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"263\" height=\"22\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/7/ec712c4ff450efe7e72962ea9782ef4afdfdb5d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-2)\\mid 99-r^{k-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"22\" />. This does not hold for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af4c200ec9851c5d84686476c5422b792db4f005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^k=3^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> does not divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e050da0534055c316c0e54b45b95b4d925994ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99-3^4=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />. This leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/e/8cef5b1869cfe84e8bff6769318769bc35ecacba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^k=9^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> as the only option. \n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/7930e74d5266daad3b606d6afd464efe38a5590f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=9$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3359f43f0fd0ed3b672d389374aecd0360921a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, we check: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/f/1afeffb66df3a39c6cd04789513fd07795926457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k-1}= a_2 = r =9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eeaed69bfe2918a11982fc05aca1b986cd3c8faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k-1}= b_2 = 91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/b/e1bbb611d01ee3a3bfa1e2c8f23ce167d650d74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=90$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/7/727c4e2b3c675d78e8654727723b7437bdaebb8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1}=a_4 = r^3 = 729$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb7682d61d6f6990e595d91d3cef573dee4c9347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+1}=b_4 = 1+3d = 271$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"200\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46abb4c7da1ffb4bb7197eeebc0e89ac54d7f9e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_{k+1}=c_4=a_4+b_4 = 729+271=1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"315\" height=\"18\" />; so it works! Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/7/2f7f4c0294c14f444de422be214b5f7285a313bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k = c_3 = 9^2+181 = 262$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the same reasoning (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> isn't very big), we can guess which terms will work. The first case is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3359f43f0fd0ed3b672d389374aecd0360921a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, so we assume the second and fourth terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the common ratio of the geometric sequence and write the arithmetic relationships in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>The common difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/32266728dcb68c87b96e7da002da972a721e1c88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100-r - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />, and so we can equate: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d76a7c1075af659d1432971c387867af97ce0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(99-r)+100-r=1000-r^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"250\" height=\"19\" />. Moving all the terms to one side and the constants to the other yields\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/3919823269433c38b1c43ce7f0786fabcbae961f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^3-3r = 702$\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/536b356c629319507c1326c52a9f2aaac3ece7e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r(r^2-3) = 702$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" />. Simply listing out the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae2f549965059c7e2b65c4366cfe542fc8fb8789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$702$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> shows that the only factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less than a square that works is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d15d808807bfa561e72dc8111649ed0a204ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/7930e74d5266daad3b606d6afd464efe38a5590f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=9$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> and we solve from there to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/4/464dea3cf637ec34ce089250dbef3a86c95d3d04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{262}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Solution by rocketscience\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28More_Robust_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(More_Robust_Bash)\">Solution 4 (More Robust Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (More Robust Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The reason for bashing in this context can also be justified by the fact 100 isn't very big. \n</p><p>Let the common difference for the arithmetic sequence be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and the common ratio for the geometric sequence be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. The sequences are now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e97f6207d32b217ad7696c0bb2b5621e2c624c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, a+1, 2a+1, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"144\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7edfe2bd738bc5ad8a482a4686a9d875e2abee1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, b, b^2, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />. We can now write the given two equations as the following:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a62340fc47df24a7cd47e2cc1ef5b9b39bea9c5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+(k-2)a+b^{k-2} = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/61351af63060957caf9c22ae5b976c39b9ecb5d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+ka+b^k = 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Take the difference between the two equations to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/826a31894d50ed30b667ccc0f12aa7bed4955d27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a+(b^2-1)b^{k-2} = 900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" />. Since 900 is divisible by 4, we can tell <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is odd. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957b560586e337ba0450a2903e996f852806079f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2m$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c5aa416b011d5980b6a7f85ba187864cf08f1e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers. Substitute variables and divide by 4 to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f197e51fa21b5d3d1190abf2294172befcb4af2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+(n+1)(n)(2n+1)^{k-2} = 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"261\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Because very small integers for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> yield very big results, we can bash through all cases of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Here, we set an upper bound for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> by setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> as 3. After trying values, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/4/b44e8f51ab12f30f9e1995e9c51e07b12e47e781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\leq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c6349b3c80b259402949015f7e90b3aadd0e1a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=9, 7, 5, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />. Testing out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15cc8804d5482ae978d97e7912aa9c768329ad49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=9$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> yields the correct answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/4/464dea3cf637ec34ce089250dbef3a86c95d3d04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{262}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. Note that even if this answer were associated with another b value like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/626beed3a7eee094ce4b6cf79a49d81669f72d99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> can still only be 3 for all of the cases.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Casework)\">Solution 5 (Casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd01cdc48042ce7c67d8edcd4904809831cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be in the form of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f77ba223af74ba4c71c0a51083bdc16a055ae31.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{array}[b]{ c c c c c c c } n &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 &amp; 6 \\\\[2ex] a_n &amp; 1 &amp; a+1 &amp; 2a+1 &amp; 3a+1 &amp; 4a+1 &amp; 5a+1 \\\\[2ex] b_n &amp; 1 &amp; b &amp; b^2 &amp; b^3 &amp; b^4 &amp; b^5 \\\\[2ex] c_n &amp; 2 &amp; b+a+1 &amp; b^2+2a+1 &amp; b^3+3a+1 &amp; b^4+4a+1 &amp; b^5+5a+1 \\end{array}\" width=\"547\" height=\"118\" />\nCase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/6/f06f024d7468691fb0e2bfd11d10076281ba7172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.\\hspace{10mm}   k = 3\\hspace{5mm} (c_1=2 \\implies k &gt; 2).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"291\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/1/a5152cab83668094d8ac6dcf2d0ad693157754f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c_2 = a+1 + b = 100, c_4 = 3a+1 + b^3 = 1000 \\implies b^3 -3b -2 = 1000-300 \\implies   b^3 - 3b = 702 \\implies b = 9, a=90, c_3 = \\boxed {262}.\\]\" width=\"933\" height=\"23\" />\nCase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/438b43ca1ee7a3e37b6bb449cc2ddf7bde532462.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2. \\hspace{10mm}   k = 4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f036b0ad501a69b424d8f6cda1b3774eba9c15de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c_3 = 2a+1 + b^2 = 100, c_5 = 4a+1 + b^4 = 1000 \\implies b^4 -2b^2 -1 = 1000-200 \\implies   b^4 - 2b^2 = 801 \\implies \\O.\\]\" width=\"791\" height=\"19\" />\nCase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f30f26744078a0d4a9e1316ba2dba67a439bfd9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3. \\hspace{10mm}   k \\ge 5.\\hspace{3mm}  b^5 &lt; 1000 \\implies b = \\{2,3\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"333\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cf0df5fc1ece2e457b409089a3836ee35bec476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.1.\\hspace{10mm} b = 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"124\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/228e70e65573678349a51c962bac5b6af8ce5e65.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c_{k-1} = 2^{k-2} + (k-2) a + 1 = 100, c_{k+1} = 2^k + ka + 1 = 1000\\implies a = 450-3\\cdot 2^{k-3} \\implies 2^k +450k -3k\\cdot 2^{k-3} + 1 = 1000  \\implies \\O.\\]\" width=\"951\" height=\"20\" />\nCase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/efffa6932655351b9f26260a44f392e0f4c1e3c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.2.\\hspace{10mm} b = 3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"124\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae77f0ba1586ef90799528633f64ec62f918beae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c_{k-1} = 3^{k-2} + (k-2) a + 1 = 100, c_{k+1} = 3^k + ka + 1 = 1000\\implies a = 450-4\\cdot 3^{k-2} \\implies 3^{k-4}(9-4k) +50k = 3\\cdot 37  \\implies \\O.\\]\" width=\"916\" height=\"20\" />\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II\" title=\"2016 AIME II\">2016 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2016\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017233832\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.050 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.068 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 582/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1808/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 130/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18692/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.213      1 -total\n 58.98%    7.203      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.30%    4.799      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14886:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017233832 and revision id 188498. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}